# Lively Dirge, "up to two": the creatures are chosen one at a time and Bot1 stops after the first (the second choice is
# declined), so one of the two eligible Gorillas returns and the other stays in the graveyard. Before that, a Dirge cast
# for mode 1 alone ({1}{B}+{1} = 3 mana) on turn 3 searches for a Gorilla and puts it into the graveyard; no creature is
# returned by it (mode 2 was not chosen), which the checks at the start of turn 5 show.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Swamp
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Lively Dirge
Lively Dirge
Entomb
Guerrilla Gorilla
Guerrilla Gorilla
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Entomb.Cast
Bot1.Search(Guerrilla Gorilla)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Lively Dirge.Cast
Bot1.Modes(1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#2.Activate
Bot1.Search(Guerrilla Gorilla)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 4
? Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 4
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lively Dirge.Cast
Bot1.Modes(2)
Bot1.Choose(Guerrilla Gorilla)
Bot1.Choose()
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Swamp; Swamp; Swamp; Mox Jet; Mox Pearl; Guerrilla Gorilla
Bot1.Graveyard = Lively Dirge; Lively Dirge; Guerrilla Gorilla; Entomb
